{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Merged as 2311. All four findings addressed:\n\n1. docs/local-dev-env.md said the sandbox permits writes to the venv; the shipped allow-list deliberately EXCLUDES it. Corrected, with the reason stated.\n2. A missing allow-list path was dropped with a bare continue. It now names the path it skipped — silently, a caller who forgot to create a directory saw only a confusing write failure from inside the sandbox with nothing pointing at the cause.\n3. The CI fail-open warning now names the variable AND its observed value. Ambient CI remains the SOLE condition (f11d-f8fd owns tightening it), so the log is the only place a reader can tell a run had no sandbox at all.\n4. docs/mutation-testing.md records what the sandbox does NOT restrict: reads and network are open by design, because write-denial was the hazard and is the scope. Now a decision rather than an accident.\n\nBoth new warnings proven RED by real mutation: removing the missing-path warning failed its test; dropping the CI value from the warning failed its test. Local run 15339 passed, 0 failed.\n\nCI note: patch set 1 failed on ubuntu py3.12 in tests/unit/test_pinned_ticket_view.py, unrelated to this change. Root-caused rather than retried blindly: line 642 is a SETUP precondition asserting the ticket blob is stored LOOSE, and rebar deliberately no longer pins gc.auto=0, so an auto gc can pack it and the test fails before exercising anything. Filed as 7bcc-55a9-7a28-412d. py3.11 and py3.13 passed on identical code, the test passed locally four times, and the recheck run was fully green."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787897496863087001,"uuid":"7508cb5f-b2e8-4e96-b0ba-e74e99754fd8"}